  "summary": {
    "en": "Cameroon has expanded its BIR rapid-intervention force around Lake Chad and is using drones and joint border patrols to target Anglophone separatists in the Northwest and Southwest, where attacks on government forces continue. Government troops killed four suspected separatists after a deadly village attack, and the government suspended Issa Tchiroma’s political party for three months. A military officer denounced the Martinez Zogo murder probe as a masquerade. The conflict caused 231 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.",
